# Module map for audit-modular-monolith / check-module-boundaries.py
# Model: kgrzybek/modular-monolith-with-ddd — module = bounded context = own assembly set + own schema.
#
# <module-id> <name> <namespace-root> <owns-data> <published-contract-assembly> <allowed-deps>
M1 Geography  Weather.Modules.Geography  yes  Weather.Modules.Geography.IntegrationEvents  BuildingBlocks.Domain, BuildingBlocks.Application
M2 Weather    Weather.Modules.Weather    no   Weather.Modules.Weather.IntegrationEvents    BuildingBlocks.Domain, BuildingBlocks.Application
M3 Journal    Weather.Modules.Journal    yes  Weather.Modules.Journal.IntegrationEvents    BuildingBlocks.Domain, BuildingBlocks.Application

# Rule: a module may reference another module ONLY via its *.IntegrationEvents assembly.
# Rule: modules communicate only asynchronously via the Events Bus (no direct cross-module method calls).

# Schemas / data ownership (one SQLite file per persisting module)
# M1 Geography -> GeographyContext  db: geography.db   tables: Countries, Cities
# M2 Weather   -> (none)            external OpenWeatherMap only
# M3 Journal   -> JournalContext    db: journal.db     tables: FavoriteCities, WeatherNotes, CityProjections

# Async integration edges
# M1 -> M3  CityAddedIntegrationEvent
# M2 -> (none)  Weather resolves the city via the provider (q={city},{country}); no module edge
